==Finnish==

===Etymology===
The singular instructive case of {{m|fi|kuka}}. Originally a lesser used variant of {{m|fi|kuin}}; modern differences between the two were introduced when the language was standardized.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation}}

===Conjunction===
{{fi-con}}

# [[when]], [[as]] {{gloss|temporal: at the same time or instant that}}
#: ''Sain viestisi, '''kun''' olin jo matkalla lentokentälle.''
#:: I got your message '''when''' I was already on my way to the airport.
#: ''Hän ilmestyi antamaan ohjeita, '''kun''' olin jo saanut työn valmiiksi.''
#:: He showed up to give instructions '''when''' I had already finished the job.
# [[as soon as]], [[once]]; {{n-g|expresses that the event of the main clause takes place immediately after that of the subclause, often used with the clitic {{m|fi|-han}}}}
#: ''Tulen tapaamaan sinua, '''kun'''(han) saan tämän valmiiksi.''
#:: I will come to see you '''as soon as''' I finish this job.
#  [[because]], [[since]]
#: ''Hän menetti työpaikkansa, '''kun''' tuli aina myöhässä.''
#:: She lost her job '''because''' she was always late.
#: ''En voi tulla huomenna, minulla '''kun''' on aamuvuoro.''
#:: I cannot come tomorrow '''as''' I have the morning shift.
# {{short for|fi|kunpa}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|fi|ei kun}}
* {{l|fi|kunpa}}
* {{l|fi|silloin kun}}
* {{l|fi|sitten kun}}
* {{l|fi|vittuku}}
* {{l|fi|voi kun}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|fi|kuin}}
* {{l|fi|kunnes}}

===Pronoun===
{{fi-pron}}

# {{lb|fi|relative|colloquial}} [[that]], [[who]], [[which]], [[where]]
#: ''Täällä on eräs mies, '''kun''' haluaisi tavata johtajaa.''
#: ''Täällä on eräs mies, {{l|fi|joka}} haluaisi tavata johtajaa.'' {{qualifier|standard}}
#:: There's somebody here '''who''''d like to see the boss.
#: {{syn|fi|joka}}
#: ''Kuka se on, '''kun''' huutaa?''
#: ''Kuka se on, '''ken''' huutaa?''
#:: Who is that '''who''' is shouting?
#: {{syn|fi|ken}}

